''Stellostomites'':

:'''Emended diagnosis''': weakly scleritized, disk-like body with convex dorsal and concave ventral surface. The ali- mentary canal enclosed in a dextrally coiled sac with bifurcated tentacles surrounding the mouth, mouth and anus close each other and open to outside through sub-triangular orifice on the ventral surface of the central dome-like cavity. Dorsal radiating canals extend from the disc margin through the upper surface to the top of the central cavity. Ventral lobes radiate from a central ring through the lower surface to the disc margin with auxiliary lobes in between in the out zone of the disc.
:'''Remarks:''' Stellostomites Sun &amp; Hou differs from El- donia Walcott in arrangement of lobes. In Eldonia, radiating lobes bifurcate at the margin of the disc, giving about 60 slightly projecting rounded lappets, whereas, in Stellosto- mites, the secondary lobation occurs in between the lobes on the margin of the disc. In addition, Eldonia lacks dorsal radiating canals and central cavity as in Stellostomites.

''S. eumorphus'':

:'''Emended diagnosis:''' woft, round disk-like body with convex dorsal and concave ventral surface, faint concentric ornaments on dorsal surface, diameter ranges from 28–110 mm. Dorsal radiating canals 88 in number, ventral lobes 44 in number. Ventral surface with regular pattern of ‘black spots’ arranged in pairs radically on the ventral surface of body.

''Pararotadiscus'':

:'''Emended diagnosis:''' round disk-like body with moderately scleritized convex dorsal surface and soft concave ventral surface, distinct radiating and concentric ornaments on the dorsal surface. Dorsal surface gradually scleritizes during growth. The alimentary canal enclosed in a dextrally coiled sac with bifurcated tentacles surrounding the mouth, mouth and anus close each other. Radiating lobes radiate from a central ring to the disc margin with secondary lobes in the out zone of the disc, the mesenteries separating the lobes septa-like pending on the inner surface of the dorsal disc.
:'''Remarks:''' Pararotadiscus nov. gen. is similar to Rota- discus Sun &amp; Hou in having scleritized dorsal surface, but differs from latter in having plate-like mesenteries, and in having soft dorsal surface in juveniles and less degree of sclerization of the dorsal surface in adults. In addition, tentacles of Rotadiscus do not show bifurcation. Pararota- discus nov. gen. is similar to Eldonia Walcott, both have similar lobe structures and tentacles, but Eldonia has a very soft dorsal surface of disc.

''P. guizhouensis''

:'''Emended diagnosis:''' round disc-like body, 15–105 mm
in diameter, with radiating and concentric ornaments on moderately scleritized convex dorsal surface, the ornaments more distinct in the inner zone and outer zone of the disc. About 40 radiating lobes radiate from a central ring to the disc margin with secondary lobes in the out zone of the disc. The mesenteries separating the lobes stiff and plate-like, become soft in the marginal zone of the disc.

