''Pararotadiscus'':

:"Although numerous specimens exhibit obvious plastic deformation resulting from compaction, folding of discs is rare, indicating that the disc of P. guizhouensis was probably softer than that of Rotadiscus grandis (Zhu et al., 2002)."
